  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing recorded $13.3B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Award activity includes 15,403 obligations with an average award size of $861K. Obligations are up 1.4% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a peak at $34.4B in FY22, with FY21 at $19.5B, FY23 at $12.8B, FY24 at $10.1B, and FY25 at $13.1B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer with $12.3B in obligations for FY2026 to date. MCKESSON CORPORATION is the dominant vendor with $12.3B in obligations for FY2026 to date. Other meaningful buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $692M and the Department of Justice at $201M. Other notable vendors include EMERGENT BIOSOLUTIONS CANADA INC at $118M and PHLOW CORP. at $105M. This profile shows concentration in both buying and supplying within the NAICS 325412 federal market for the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What happened to spending over time?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year obligations rose to $34.4B in FY22 and then fell to $12.8B in FY23. Obligations continued lower at $10.1B in FY24 and then moved up to $13.1B in FY25. Obligations are $13.3B for FY26 to date, representing an increase of up 1.4% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who dominates buying and contracting in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $12.3B for FY2026 to date. MCKESSON CORPORATION obligated $12.3B as the top vendor for FY2026 to date, with EMERGENT BIOSOLUTIONS CANADA INC at $118M and PHLOW CORP. at $105M following. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $692M and the Department of Justice obligated $201M in FY2026 to date."
      }
    ]
